1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,951
hello! Today we will learn expressions used at an alley restaurant in Gamcheon Culture Village.

2
00:00:05,951 --> 00:00:09,489
Do you have any idea what to say at a Korean restaurant?

3
00:00:09,489 --> 00:00:15,600
Once you learn them one by one, you can confidently order from anywhere. Let’s go together!

4
00:00:16,050 --> 00:00:24,271
As I walked through the alley, I felt hungry. At times like this, we say, ‘I’m hungry.’

5
00:00:24,271 --> 00:00:33,790
‘Bae’ means hungry, and ‘I’m hungry’ means I need food. Find a delicious restaurant.

6
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:43,678
There is an order in a restaurant. ‘Find’ a restaurant, ‘order’, express ‘taste’, ‘calculate’.

7
00:00:43,678 --> 00:00:50,420
Today we will learn these four steps along with expressions appropriate for the situation.

8
00:00:50,870 --> 00:00:56,636
In an unfamiliar neighborhood, you don't know where the food is delicious. Ask someone passing by.

9
00:00:56,636 --> 00:01:02,870
‘Is there a good restaurant near here’? Please kindly tell me this.

10
00:01:03,320 --> 00:01:09,471
If it's difficult to choose, ask them to choose. ‘Is there a restaurant you can recommend?’

11
00:01:09,471 --> 00:01:13,400
‘Recommendation’ means selecting something good and telling it to you.

12
00:01:13,850 --> 00:01:20,607
If you're curious about popular food in your neighborhood, ask 'What's famous here?' I ask.

13
00:01:20,607 --> 00:01:25,230
‘Famous’ means that many people like it.

14
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:32,360
If you're curious about what's for sale, ask 'What is this house for sale'? I ask.

15
00:01:32,360 --> 00:01:39,220
‘Sell’ means selling. You can ask in advance before entering.

16
00:01:39,670 --> 00:01:44,902
If the menu looks appetizing, we say, ‘It looks delicious.’

17
00:01:44,902 --> 00:01:52,750
'-It looks like' means it feels that way when you see it. Come into this restaurant!

18
00:01:53,200 --> 00:02:00,929
When you enter, the clerk asks. ‘How many are you?’ ‘How many people are there’? It means.

19
00:02:00,929 --> 00:02:03,690
Checking the number of guests.

20
00:02:04,140 --> 00:02:13,331
If you're alone, it's 'one person', if you're together, it's 'two people'. ‘Myeong’ is a word for counting people.

21
00:02:13,331 --> 00:02:17,820
It's more clear if you show the number with your fingers.

22
00:02:18,270 --> 00:02:25,836
When you see an empty seat, do you think, ‘Can I sit here?’ I ask. ‘-Can I have a baby’?

23
00:02:25,836 --> 00:02:31,810
means asking for permission. If you say ‘yes’, you can sit down.

24
00:02:32,260 --> 00:02:37,509
Once you sit down, you need a menu. ‘Please give me the menu’.

25
00:02:37,509 --> 00:02:44,070
‘Menu’ is a list of food, and ‘please’ is a polite request.

26
00:02:44,520 --> 00:02:50,105
If you don't know what to choose, ask yourself, 'What's delicious here?' I ask.

27
00:02:50,105 --> 00:02:54,120
You can get recommendations on things that the house is good at.

28
00:02:54,570 --> 00:03:00,639
If you're curious about what's ordered a lot, ask 'What's the popular menu?' I ask.

29
00:03:00,639 --> 00:03:03,760
Popular menu items usually never fail.

30
00:03:04,210 --> 00:03:10,968
If you have trouble choosing, ask the clerk, “Please recommend a menu.”

31
00:03:10,968 --> 00:03:14,910
It means ‘Please choose for me.’

32
00:03:15,360 --> 00:03:27,168
Point to food you see for the first time and ask, ‘What is this?’ I ask. ‘This’ is ‘This’.

33
00:03:27,168 --> 00:03:30,120
Ask any questions you have.

34
00:03:30,570 --> 00:03:36,424
If you are curious about the material, ask ‘What is this made from?’ I ask.

35
00:03:36,424 --> 00:03:40,150
Be sure to check if there are any ingredients you cannot eat.

36
00:03:40,600 --> 00:03:51,259
The ingredients are usually like this. ‘Rice’, ‘meat’, ‘vegetables’, and ‘seafood’ like fish.

37
00:03:51,259 --> 00:03:55,430
Most people understand these four things.

38
00:03:55,880 --> 00:04:04,520
If you're curious about the taste, ask 'What does this taste like?' I ask. It's easy to choose if you know the taste in advance.

39
00:04:04,970 --> 00:04:09,187
If you can't eat spicy food, be sure to ask. ‘Is this spicy’?

40
00:04:09,187 --> 00:04:13,560
This is a very important question because Korean food is very spicy.

41
00:04:14,010 --> 00:04:21,489
To avoid spicy food, ‘Is there anything that isn’t spicy?’ I ask.

42
00:04:21,489 --> 00:04:27,280
‘An’ means ‘not’, that is, it is not spicy.

43
00:04:27,730 --> 00:04:37,500
If you share or are hungry, is it ‘too much’? I ask. ‘Amount’ is the amount of food.

44
00:04:37,950 --> 00:04:43,852
Once you've made your choice, point to it and say 'Please give me this' to finish ordering.

45
00:04:43,852 --> 00:04:50,410
‘This’ is the most commonly used spelling expression.

46
00:04:50,860 --> 00:05:03,000
Also tell me the number. ‘Please give me one of this and two of that.’ If it's close, it's 'this', and if it's far, it's 'that'.

47
00:05:03,450 --> 00:05:13,410
If you are thirsty, say, ‘Give me some water.’ Water is free at Korean restaurants. If you add 'jom', it becomes softer.

48
00:05:13,860 --> 00:05:20,502
The food is here! Before eating, say, ‘I will eat well.’

49
00:05:20,502 --> 00:05:24,800
It is an expression of gratitude to the person who made it.

50
00:05:25,250 --> 00:05:35,380
If there aren't enough side dishes, 'Please give me more side dishes.' ‘More’ is addition. Side dishes are usually provided for free.

51
00:05:35,830 --> 00:05:41,058
If you don't have a spoon, 'Please give me chopsticks and a spoon.'

52
00:05:41,058 --> 00:05:46,940
‘Chopsticks’ means picking up, and ‘spoon’ means scooping.

53
00:05:47,390 --> 00:05:55,620
If I want to eat more, ‘Can I refill this?’ ‘Refill’ means to refill.

54
00:05:56,070 --> 00:06:04,223
Express the taste. If it’s delicious, it’s ‘delicious’! When you raise your thumb, your feelings are conveyed more.

55
00:06:04,223 --> 00:06:07,280
This is a huge compliment to the person who made it.

56
00:06:07,730 --> 00:06:19,610
Spicy taste is ‘spicy’, salty taste is ‘salty’. If you add ‘a little’, it becomes soft — ‘a little spicy.’

57
00:06:20,060 --> 00:06:28,890
If the taste is sweet, it will be ‘sweet’, if the seasoning is weak, it will be ‘bland’. Each taste has a different expression.

58
00:06:29,340 --> 00:06:39,320
A clean taste is ‘light’, and a savory taste like sesame oil is ‘savory’. It's perfect for complimenting the soup.

59
00:06:39,770 --> 00:06:41,861
Taste expression summary!

60
00:06:41,861 --> 00:06:53,622
‘Spicy’, ‘salty’, ‘sweet’, ‘sour’, ‘bitter’, ‘bland’, ‘savory’,

61
00:06:53,622 --> 00:06:59,110
‘Feel’. You can use it according to the situation.

62
00:07:06,960 --> 00:07:10,672
If you ate it all, you ate well.

63
00:07:10,672 --> 00:07:20,060
Before eating, say, ‘I will eat well,’ and after eating, say, ‘I ate well.’ I remember them as a pair.

64
00:07:20,510 --> 00:07:29,200
If you have leftovers, can you please pack the leftovers? ‘Cheap’ means packaging.

65
00:07:29,650 --> 00:07:40,256
When you're done eating, go to the counter and say, 'I'll pay, how much is it?' ‘Calculate’ means putting a price on it, ‘how much is it?’

66
00:07:40,256 --> 00:07:42,420
is to ask about the price.

67
00:07:42,870 --> 00:07:52,950
If it's a card, 'Can it be a card?' , if it is cash, ‘I will pay in cash’. Some small stores only accept cash.

68
00:07:53,400 --> 00:08:00,240
If you need a receipt, say ‘Please give me a receipt.’ It's a piece of paper that says how much you paid.

69
00:08:00,690 --> 00:08:09,230
If it was delicious, 'It was really delicious here, I want to come again'! A warm word becomes a good memory.

70
00:08:09,680 --> 00:08:21,124
Let’s take a look at today’s trend. Find, order, taste, checkout. Now you know what words to use in each situation, right?

71
00:08:21,124 --> 00:08:23,460
Well done!

72
00:08:23,910 --> 00:08:31,405
Be sure to use the expressions you learned today at a restaurant. The more you use it, the more natural it becomes.

73
00:08:31,405 --> 00:08:35,360
Next, let’s learn cafe expressions. hi!

